    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-06eac70e810c\",\"class\":\"partial\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"placeholder-function-declaration-name\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\bfunction\\\\s+(foo|bar|baz|qux|doStuff|doSomething|doIt|myFunction|myFunc|func\\\\d*|fn\\\\d*|temp|tmp|asdf|test\\\\d+)\\\\s*\\\\(\",\"path\":\".floor/added-lines.txt\"},{\"id\":\"placeholder-function-expression-name\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\b(const|let|var)\\\\s+(foo|bar|baz|qux|doStuff|doSomething|doIt|myFunction|myFunc|func\\\\d*|fn\\\\d*|temp|tmp|asdf|test\\\\d+)\\\\s*=\\\\s*(async\\\\s*)?(\\\\(|function\\\\b)\",\"path\":\".floor/added-lines.txt\"}],\"coverage\":\"Flagrant violations only: an added function declaration, or an added const/let/var bound to a function or arrow function, whose name is a placeholder such as foo, bar, doStuff, doSomething, myFunction, fn1, func2, temp, tmp, asdf or test1. A placeholder name cannot describe what any function does.\",\"residual\":\"Does each function added or renamed in this diff have a name that accurately describes what its body actually does, and not a misleading, vague or outdated description?\",\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/app/helpers.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\\n+export function doStuff(x: number): number {\\n+  return x * 2;\\n+}\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/app/helpers2.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1 @@\\n+export const foo = (a: number): number => a * 2;\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/app/order-total.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\\n+export function computeOrderTotal(prices: number[]): number {\\n+  return prices.reduce((sum, p) => sum + p, 0);\\n+}\\n+export const doubleAmount = (a: number): number => a * 2;\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"Whether a name matches a function's behaviour depends on what the code means, so a pattern cannot decide it. Placeholder names in added function declarations or function-valued bindings can never describe behaviour, so they are flagrant, mechanically detectable violations. Misleading, vague or stale descriptive names are left to the residual question.\"}",
